# RemoteLogManager.java & RemoteStorageMetrics.java Changes (KAFKA-20157)

## 1. RemoteStorageMetrics.java — Constant Additions

Two private name constants were added:
```java
private static final String RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT = "RetentionSizeInPercent";
private static final String LOCAL_RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT = "LocalRetentionSizeInPercent";
```

Two public `MetricName` fields, both built for type `"RemoteLogManager"` under domain `"kafka.log.remote"`:
```java
public static final MetricName RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT_METRIC = getMetricName(
        "kafka.log.remote", "RemoteLogManager", RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT);
public static final MetricName LOCAL_RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT_METRIC = getMetricName(
        "kafka.log.remote", "RemoteLogManager", LOCAL_RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT);
```

## 2. RLMExpirationTask — Field Declarations

```java
private volatile boolean metricsRegistered = false;
private final Map<String, String> metricTags = new HashMap<>();
private final AtomicInteger retentionSizeInPercentValue = new AtomicInteger(0);
private final AtomicInteger localRetentionSizeInPercentValue = new AtomicInteger(0);
```

Accessors (visible for testing) return the current `AtomicInteger` values via `.get()`. In the constructor, tags are populated with `topic` and `partition` (partition converted via `Integer.toString(...)`).

## 3. registerMetrics() — Gauge Registration with Tags

Guarded so it only runs once and only when the task is not cancelled:
```java
void registerMetrics() {
    if (!metricsRegistered && !isCancelled()) {
        metricsGroup.newGauge(RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT_METRIC.getName(), retentionSizeInPercentValue::get, metricTags);
        metricsGroup.newGauge(LOCAL_RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT_METRIC.getName(), localRetentionSizeInPercentValue::get, metricTags);
        metricsRegistered = true;
    }
}
```
It is invoked at the start of `execute(...)`, described as running `"on first execution (after task is safely scheduled)"`.

## 4. cancel() — Reset and Remove Metrics

On cancel, values are reset to zero and gauges are removed if previously registered:
```java
retentionSizeInPercentValue.set(0);
localRetentionSizeInPercentValue.set(0);
if (metricsRegistered) {
    metricsGroup.removeMetric(RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT_METRIC.getName(), metricTags);
    metricsGroup.removeMetric(LOCAL_RETENTION_SIZE_IN_PERCENT_METRIC.getName(), metricTags);
    metricsRegistered = false;
}
super.cancel();
```

## 5. calculateSizeInPercent() — The Computation

A new private helper computes both percentages as integers, returning 0 when the relevant retention limit is not positive:
```java
private void calculateSizeInPercent(long totalSize, long retentionSize,
                                    long localLogSegmentsSize, long localRetentionBytes) {
    int sizePercentage = retentionSize > 0 ? (int) ((totalSize * 100) / retentionSize) : 0;
    retentionSizeInPercentValue.set(sizePercentage);
    int localSizePercentage = localRetentionBytes > 0 ? (int) ((localLogSegmentsSize * 100) / localRetentionBytes) : 0;
    localRetentionSizeInPercentValue.set(localSizePercentage);
}
```

## 6. buildRetentionSizeData() — Signature and Logic Changes

The method gained two new parameters: `localLogSegmentsSize` and `localRetentionBytes`. The early-return logic was restructured so the negative case returns first, and the "within limits" case now computes percentages before returning empty:
```java
if (retentionSize < 0) {
    return Optional.empty();
}
long totalEstimateSize = onlyLocalLogSegmentsSize + fullCopyFinishedSegmentsSizeInBytes;
if (totalEstimateSize <= retentionSize) {
    calculateSizeInPercent(totalEstimateSize, retentionSize, localLogSegmentsSize, localRetentionBytes);
    return Optional.empty();
}
```

Later, after computing `totalSize` (local segments + remote log size), the percentage is calculated before the breach check:
```java
long totalSize = onlyLocalLogSegmentsSize + remoteLogSizeBytes;
calculateSizeInPercent(totalSize, retentionSize, localLogSegmentsSize, localRetentionBytes);
if (totalSize > retentionSize) { ... }
```

## 7. Related Callers

- The zero-metadata branch now calls `calculateSizeInPercent(log.size(), log.config().retentionSize, log.size(), log.config().localRetentionBytes())`.
- The main caller passes the new arguments including `log.size()` and `log.config().localRetentionBytes()`.
- An `import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;` and static imports for the two new metric constants were added.

---
*Note:* Percentages are integer-truncated (e.g., `84`, `107`, `50`). Values can exceed 100 when actual size surpasses the configured retention limit.

